{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44116398",
      "title": "Adding Links The Right Way",
      "lectureOrder": 271,
      "videoOrder": 259,
      "sourceHash": "abb37da38bf119b0564957e4d7ceb720141fedb150a8a9d4fc74677ed31d2f9e",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.72,
          "end": 1.65,
          "en": "So let's make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.65,
          "end": 3.99,
          "en": "that we got some actual links here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 3.99,
          "end": 6.75,
          "en": "that load different routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 6.75,
          "end": 10.456,
          "en": "And for that, I'll go to my users component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.456,
          "end": 14.82,
          "en": "And there it's actually the user component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.82,
          "end": 15.963,
          "en": "which I want to visit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.55,
          "end": 19.47,
          "en": "So this component here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.47,
          "end": 22.74,
          "en": "Because it's in there in the template of this component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.74,
          "end": 26.979,
          "en": "where I already am rendering an anchor tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 26.979,
          "end": 31.979,
          "en": "So I already do have links here for these user items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 33.09,
          "end": 37.02,
          "en": "but at the moment, these links aren't doing anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 37.02,
          "end": 39.78,
          "en": "This anchor tag has no configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.78,
          "end": 42.963,
          "en": "that would cause it to trigger a navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 44.07,
          "end": 47.1,
          "en": "And we can of course change that by adding",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 47.1,
          "end": 50.1,
          "en": "the href attribute here, for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 54.93,
          "en": "And by setting this to a path we wanna navigate to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.93,
          "end": 57.42,
          "en": "because that's how links work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 57.42,
          "end": 62.42,
          "en": "So here we could want to navigate to /tasks for example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 62.701,
          "end": 67.701,
          "en": "Later we might want to make sure that the user ID is kind",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 73.25,
          "en": "of encoded in the URL so that we can load different tasks",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 73.35,
          "end": 74.64,
          "en": "for different users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.64,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "But for the moment to keep it simple, I'll just navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 79.863,
          "en": "to tasks like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.05,
          "end": 86.43,
          "en": "With that, if we save this, we can click those users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.43,
          "end": 89.163,
          "en": "and you see the URL updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.45,
          "end": 92.85,
          "en": "But you'll also see something else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 92.85,
          "end": 97.85,
          "en": "Every time I click a user, the app briefly flickers here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 98.67,
          "end": 101.4,
          "en": "So it looks like the entire page is reloading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 101.4,
          "end": 102.993,
          "en": "on every navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 104.16,
          "end": 106.53,
          "en": "In addition, if you open the developer tools,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 106.53,
          "end": 109.74000000000001,
          "en": "and you go to the network tab, you will notice",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 109.74000000000001,
          "end": 111.72,
          "en": "that for every navigation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 111.72,
          "end": 115.28999999999999,
          "en": "all these files here are loaded again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 115.28999999999999,
          "end": 117.3,
          "en": "So the entire page is loaded again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.3,
          "end": 120.72,
          "en": "and all the JavaScript files are loaded again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 120.72,
          "end": 123.213,
          "en": "And that happens for every navigation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.77,
          "end": 128.43,
          "en": "And that's not ideal because since we're",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 128.43,
          "end": 132.557,
          "en": "in a single page application where Angular is powering",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 132.557,
          "end": 136.12,
          "en": "the UI, it would be nice if we could stay",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 136.12,
          "end": 138.63,
          "en": "in that single page application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 138.63,
          "end": 141.93,
          "en": "And if we wouldn't unnecessarily reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.93,
          "end": 145.71,
          "en": "the page all the time because refetching",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 145.71,
          "end": 149.37,
          "en": "that same one single index HTML file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 149.37,
          "end": 151.62,
          "en": "and all the JavaScript files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 151.62,
          "end": 154.2,
          "en": "that are needed by this application over,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 154.2,
          "end": 157.02,
          "en": "and over again, does not make any sense,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 157.02,
          "end": 160.95,
          "en": "and instead leads to a worse user experience.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 160.95,
          "end": 164.1,
          "en": "Also, because refetching all these files",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 164.1,
          "end": 167.117,
          "en": "can slow our application down.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.117,
          "end": 170.82,
          "en": "That's why you typically don't want to navigate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 170.82,
          "end": 175.29,
          "en": "by using a regular link with that href attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 175.29,
          "end": 177.87,
          "en": "You could do it, but it's not the preferred way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 177.87,
          "end": 181.02,
          "en": "because it would to the page being loaded again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 181.02,
          "end": 182.553,
          "en": "and again, and again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 183.87,
          "end": 187.08,
          "en": "So instead of using this href attribute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.08,
          "end": 190.98,
          "en": "for setting up a link, you should typically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 190.98,
          "end": 195.873,
          "en": "in an Angular application, use the RouterLink directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.8,
          "end": 199.53300000000002,
          "en": "which is a directive offered by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 199.53300000000002,
          "end": 203.096,
          "en": "even though it doesn't start with ng,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.096,
          "end": 204.797,
          "en": "but it's still offered by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 204.797,
          "end": 207.51,
          "en": "And it is a directive that will",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 207.51,
          "end": 211.47,
          "en": "in the end, set up a path for this link.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 211.47,
          "end": 216,
          "en": "But Angular will then block the browser default behavior,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 216,
          "end": 220.23,
          "en": "which would be to refetch the HTML document.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 220.23,
          "end": 224.155,
          "en": "And instead Angular will take over, will take a look",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 224.155,
          "end": 227.415,
          "en": "at the path you want to navigate to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 227.415,
          "end": 230.97,
          "en": "and it will then take a look at the route configuration,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 230.97,
          "end": 234.39,
          "en": "and load and render the appropriate component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 234.39,
          "end": 238.59,
          "en": "without leaving that single page application world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 238.59,
          "end": 241.563,
          "en": "That's what RouterLink does for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 243.57,
          "end": 248.07,
          "en": "Therefore, RouterLink wants an input value, which is still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 248.07,
          "end": 250.114,
          "en": "that path you want to navigate to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 250.114,
          "end": 255.114,
          "en": "But now Angular will take over and will make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 255.33,
          "end": 258.603,
          "en": "that the appropriate content is shown on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 260.37,
          "end": 263.37,
          "en": "Now, if you would save it like this, you'd run",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 263.37,
          "end": 265.02,
          "en": "into a problem though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 265.02,
          "end": 268.65,
          "en": "If you now click on a user, nothing happens.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 268.65,
          "end": 271.56,
          "en": "And the reason for that is that, as I mentioned,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 271.56,
          "end": 275.28,
          "en": "RouterLink is a directive offered by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 275.28,
          "end": 277.23,
          "en": "But as you learned before in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 277.23,
          "end": 282.21,
          "en": "by default, out of the box directives aren't auto detected,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 282.21,
          "end": 283.69100000000003,
          "en": "or anything like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 283.69100000000003,
          "end": 287.22,
          "en": "So you must make Angular aware of the fact",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 287.22,
          "end": 289.89,
          "en": "that you're using this directive in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 289.89,
          "end": 292.71,
          "en": "and you're doing that by adding this imports array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 292.71,
          "end": 295.09000000000003,
          "en": "to that component decorator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 295.09000000000003,
          "end": 299.64,
          "en": "And there you would add the RouterLink directive,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 299.64,
          "end": 302.883,
          "en": "which must be imported from @Angular router.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 305.646,
          "end": 308.94,
          "en": "With that now done, if you save and reload, you will be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 308.94,
          "end": 313.94,
          "en": "to click on a user and you see the URL changed to /tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 314.58,
          "end": 317.133,
          "en": "But now if you switch between users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 317.133,
          "end": 319.8,
          "en": "which is currently not reflected on the UI,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 319.8,
          "end": 321.72,
          "en": "but as you click on different users,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 321.72,
          "end": 323.97,
          "en": "the page will not flicker.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 323.97,
          "end": 325.71,
          "en": "And if you take a look at the network tab,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 325.71,
          "end": 328.623,
          "en": "you see no new requests are sent.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 329.7,
          "end": 333.84000000000003,
          "en": "For that initial request from /nothing to /tasks.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 333.84000000000003,
          "end": 336,
          "en": "There is one request being sent here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 336,
          "end": 339.21,
          "en": "because some image is refetched here, but that's all.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 339.21,
          "end": 343.62,
          "en": "All the HTML and JavaScript files are not fetched again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 343.62,
          "end": 346.47,
          "en": "and that's therefore how you set up links",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 346.47,
          "end": 348.723,
          "en": "when using the Angular router.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
